=== Cultural Properties ===
List of cultural properties related to the shrine.

=== National Historic Site ===
* Mount Hōman – surrounding area including the shrine precincts. Designated October 17, 2013 <ref name="史跡"/>.

=== Fukuoka Prefecture Designated Cultural Properties ===
* Tangible Cultural Properties
** Wooden Komainu (sculpture)  
**: Discovered beneath the worship hall floor in {{ill|lt=1978|Q2483|qid=Q2483|1=1978}} <ref name="狛犬"/>. A paired A-un set carved from camphor wood, each 90 cm tall <ref name="狛犬"/>. Dated to the latter half of the {{ill|lt=15th century|Q7018|qid=Q7018|1=15th century}} <ref name="狛犬"/>. Owned by Dazaifu Tenmangū. Designated April 1, 1982 <ref name="狛犬"/>.
* Tangible Folk Cultural Properties
** Materials related to Mount Hōman mountain worship  
**: A total of 307 items held by the shrine, including ritual implements, talismans, votive offerings, paintings, and records <ref name="信仰"/>. Evaluated as valuable materials related to ancient Mount Hōman worship <ref name="信仰"/>. Among them, the Sanskrit-inscribed sacred mirrors were donated in Kan’ei 18 (1641) by {{ill|lt=Kuroda Tadayuki|Q11678600|qid=Q11678600|1=Tadayuki Kuroda}}, second lord of the Fukuoka Domain, representing the three deities of Kamado Shrine: Hōman-gū, Seibō-gū, and Hachiman-gū (the Hōman-gū mirror was lost in 1853) <ref name="信仰"/>. The Seibō-gū and Hachiman-gū mirrors are each just under 45 cm in diameter and 0.7 cm thick <ref name="信仰"/>. Designated February 20, 1962; additional designation and name change on March 18, 2011 <ref name="信仰"/>.

=== On-Site Information ===
**Location**
* Upper Shrine: Kitadani, {{ill|lt=Dazaifu City|Q728218|qid=Q728218|1=Dazaifu, Fukuoka}}, {{ill|lt=Fukuoka Prefecture|Q123258|qid=Q123258|1=Fukuoka Prefecture}} – summit of Mount Hōman.
* Lower Shrine: 883 Gokuyadani, Uchiyama, Dazaifu City, Fukuoka Prefecture

**Access (to the Lower Shrine)**
* Bus: From {{ill|lt=Dazaifu Station|Q5243657|qid=Q5243657|1=Dazaifu Station}} on the {{ill|lt=Nishitetsu Dazaifu Line|Q5243658|qid=Q5243658|1=Dazaifu Line}}, take the {{ill|lt=Mahoroba Bus|Q11278478|qid=Q11278478|1=Mahoroba-gō}} Uchiyama Line, get off at the terminal “Uchiyama,” then walk a short distance.
* Car: About 8 km from {{ill|lt=Dazaifu Interchange|Q1575734|qid=Q1575734|1=Dazaifu interchange}} on the {{ill|lt=Kyushu Expressway|Q1060803|qid=Q1060803|1=Kyushu Expressway}}.
** Paid parking available

